Isabelle tool library
===========================

This project allows MCP server developers to make their MCP server user-extensible:
users of an MCP server can define their own MCP tools by writing Isabelle/ML instead
of changing the MCP server.

To achieve this, this project implements two things:

- A reusable Scala library for the development of MCP servers that can invoke MCP tools in the verifier process
- A Isabelle/ML library to react to MCP tools invocation in the verifier

# Scala library

The Scala library API defines how the MCP server and verifier will interact
for the purpose of defining tools, invoking them and cancelling invocation.

# Isabelle/ML library

A user of this library can define MCP tools by writing Isabelle/ML programs as follows:

```
theory Example_Tools
imports
  MCP_Tools
begin

mcp_tool hello_world
  (description "Return a hello-world greeting")
  :: "unit"
  = run \<open>fn _ => fn () => "Hello, world!"\<close>

mcp_tool hello_name
  (description "Greet a person by name")
  for name "Name of the person to greet" :: "string"
  = run \<open>fn _ => fn {name} => "Hello, " ^ name ^ "!"\<close>

end
```

See the `Examples` directory for more.

# User-extensible MCP servers 

Because MCP tools can be define in theories we can now implement a user-extensible MCP server.

# Compatibility

This library is a Isabelle2025-2 component. It will be updated to newer versions of the
Isabelle theorem prover as long as the author needs it.

# What can you do

## I am a MCP server developer

Use this library in your MCP server to let your users implement their own tools. Read [DEVELOP_MCP](https://github.com/edoput/isabelle-tool-library/DEVELOP_MCP) for documentation about including this library in your MCP server.

## I am a user

There are two MCP servers that you can use.

- [edoput/isabelle-pide-mcp](https://github.com/edoput/isabelle-pide-mcp) is a fork of [PIDE MCP](https://github.com/kappelmann/isabelle-pide-mcp) that uses this library to implement /user tools/.
- [edoput/pide-mcp](https://github.com/edoput/pide-mcp) the original project from which this library was extracted.

If you want to develop your own tools you may want to read [DEVELOP_TOOL](https://github.com/edoput/isabelle-tool-library/DEVELOP_TOOL).

# History of this library

When exctracting this library from [edoput/pide-mcp](https://github.com/edoput/pide-mcp) I have decided to not preserve history. See PROVENANCE for the exact extraction source.

Standalone verification
-----------------------

Use the Isabelle installation where this component is registered:

    isabelle components -u /absolute/path/to/isabelle-tool-library
    isabelle scala /absolute/path/to/isabelle-tool-library/Tests/check_scala.scala
    isabelle build MCP-Tool-Library MCP-Tool-Library-HOL
    isabelle build -d /absolute/path/to/isabelle-tool-library/Tests MCP-Library-Inclusion

The Scala check recompiles the library and an external-package consumer with
library/server/test jars excluded from ambient dependencies. The consumer uses
explicit Isabelle/library requirements. The theory test imports only the library
HOL entry point and HOL-Library, checks for an empty initial catalogue, then
declares and invokes its own tool.
